# Carunel website — example environment configuration
#
# This is a plain static site (no build step, no bundler — see README.md),
# so this file does not get consumed automatically by a build process.
# It documents the one configurable value the site uses and the runtime
# equivalent you actually need to set.
#
# FORMSPREE_FORM_ID
# ------------------
# Public Formspree form ID for the Contact page inquiry form.
# Get one by creating a form at https://formspree.io.
#
# Because there is no build step to inject this value into the static
# HTML/JS, copy it directly into js/config.js instead:
#
#   window.CARUNEL_CONFIG = { FORMSPREE_FORM_ID: 'your-form-id' };
#
# If a GitHub Pages Actions build step is introduced later, this variable
# should be wired through a workflow secret (e.g. FORMSPREE_FORM_ID) that
# templates the value into js/config.js at deploy time, so it never has to
# be hand-edited or committed as a real value.
#
# Leaving this unset keeps the inquiry form hidden; the "Email Carunel
# Directly" link on the Contact page remains visible either way.
FORMSPREE_FORM_ID=
